 "about": "As `life-ruin` (berries at 40%; two signs in the empty house by the arrival point: fishing, smoking), and the scribe who put them up stays at the house. Residents have no minds, so the scribe's part is a fixed graph: stay at the house, eat from a large stock, sleep when tired. When the newcomer speaks to the scribe with teach, learn, read, writ, show or sign in the line, the scribe says one scripted line and teaches writing (the ordinary teach skill), at most three times. The ladder: ask the scribe -> writing -> read the signs -> fishing and smoking -> food that keeps.",
